IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `epd-nouns`

-- The ePrivacy Directive (Directive 2002/58/EC), consolidated version of 19.12.2009: Articles 14 to 21.
-- LAYER 1. Technical features (Art 14), application of Directive 95/46/EC and the restrictions Member States may adopt
-- (Art 15), implementation and enforcement (Art 15a), transitional arrangements (Art 16), the reading of references to the
-- repealed Directive (Art 19, second subparagraph) and the addressees (Art 21).
-- Not encoded, and inert as machinery (reason 2) in NOTES.md: Art 14a (the committee procedure), Art 15a(4) second
-- subparagraph (the Commission's consultation on cross-border measures), Art 17 (transposition), Art 18 (review), Art 19 first
-- subparagraph (the repeal of Directive 97/66/EC) and Art 20 (entry into force).
-- The Articles are addressed to Member States, the Commission and providers. Each function says what the DIRECTIVE requires or
-- allows, never what a particular Member State's law has done (NOTES.md).
-- JUST TRUE = the text says yes, JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words, NOTHING = not covered (NOTES.md, "Reading a
-- result: FALSE and NOTHING").

§ `Article 14 -- technical features and standardisation`

-- src:132 | In implementing the provisions of this Directive, Member States shall ensure, subject to paragraphs 2 and 3, that no mandatory requirements for specific technical features are imposed on terminal or other electronic communication equipment which could impede the placing of equipment on the market and the free circulation of such equipment in and between Member States.
@ref Art 14(1) (src:132) row:A14(1)
GIVEN `the requirement is mandatory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is for specific technical features` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is imposed on terminal or other electronic communication equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement could impede the placing of equipment on the market and the free circulation of such equipment in and between Member States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph 2 or paragraph 3 of this Article applies to the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(1) the mandatory requirement for specific technical features may be imposed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about mandatory requirements for specific technical features imposed on terminal or other electronic communication equipment which could impede the placing on the market and the free circulation of the equipment
        IF (NOT `the requirement is mandatory`) OR (NOT `the requirement is for specific technical features`) OR (NOT `the requirement is imposed on terminal or other electronic communication equipment`) OR (NOT `the requirement could impede the placing of equipment on the market and the free circulation of such equipment in and between Member States`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to paragraphs 2 and 3" -- what those paragraphs allow is not decided here
        IF `paragraph 2 or paragraph 3 of this Article applies to the requirement` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no mandatory requirements for specific technical features are imposed on terminal or other electronic communication equipment which could impede the placing of equipment on the market"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:133 | Where provisions of this Directive can be implemented only by requiring specific technical features in electronic communications networks, Member States shall inform the Commission in accordance with the procedure provided for by Directive 98/34/EC
@ref Art 14(2) (src:133) row:A14(2)
GIVEN `provisions of this Directive can be implemented only by requiring specific technical features in electronic communications networks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(2) the Member State must inform the Commission` MEANS
    IF `provisions of this Directive can be implemented only by requiring specific technical features in electronic communications networks`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where provisions of this Directive can be implemented only by requiring specific technical features in electronic communications networks" -- a "where" condition that fails (periods ruling (b)); FORK F6
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the Member State informed the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it did so in accordance with the procedure provided for by Directive 98/34/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(2) the Member State's duty to inform the Commission is met` MEANS
    IF `the Member State informed the Commission` AND `it did so in accordance with the procedure provided for by Directive 98/34/EC`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Member States shall inform the Commission in accordance with the procedure provided for by Directive 98/34/EC"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:136 | Where required, measures may be adopted to ensure that terminal equipment is constructed in a way that is compatible with the right of users to protect and control the use of their personal data, in accordance with Directive 1999/5/EC and Council Decision 87/95/EEC
@ref Art 14(3) (src:136) row:A14(3)
GIVEN `the measure is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure is to ensure that terminal equipment is constructed in a way that is compatible with the right of users to protect and control the use of their personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure is in accordance with Directive 1999/5/EC and Council Decision 87/95/EEC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 14(3) the measure may be adopted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where required" -- a "where" condition on a power that fails (periods ruling (b)); FORK F11 (grant and power ruling item 3: listed, not changed)
        IF NOT `the measure is required` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is stated for measures to ensure terminal equipment compatible with the right of users to protect and control the use of their personal data, in accordance with Directive 1999/5/EC and Decision 87/95/EEC
        IF (NOT `the measure is to ensure that terminal equipment is constructed in a way that is compatible with the right of users to protect and control the use of their personal data`) OR (NOT `the measure is in accordance with Directive 1999/5/EC and Council Decision 87/95/EEC`) THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 15 -- application of certain provisions of Directive 95/46/EC`

-- src:148 | Member States may adopt legislative measures to restrict the scope of the rights and obligations provided for in Article 5, Article 6, Article 8(1), (2), (3) and (4), and Article 9 of this Directive when such restriction constitutes a necessary, appropriate and proportionate measure within a democratic society to safeguard national security (i.e. State security), defence, public security, and the prevention, investigation, detection and prosecution of criminal offences or of unauthorised use of the electronic communication system, as referred to in Article 13(1) of Directive 95/46/EC.
@ref Art 15(1) first sentence (src:148) row:A15(1).s1
GIVEN `the measure is a legislative measure` IS A BOOLEAN
      provision IS A `Restrictable provision`
      purpose IS A `Restriction purpose`
      `the restriction constitutes a necessary, appropriate and proportionate measure within a democratic society` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(1) first sentence the Member State may adopt the legislative measure restricting the scope of the rights and obligations` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to adopt legislative measures
        IF NOT `the measure is a legislative measure` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the rights and obligations are those "provided for in Article 5, Article 6, Article 8(1), (2), (3) and (4), and Article 9"; the list is not closed with "only", so for another provision the sentence is silent
        IF provision EQUALS `another provision of this Directive` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the purposes named are national security, defence, public security and the prevention, investigation, detection and prosecution of criminal offences or of unauthorised use of the electronic communication system; the list is not closed with "only"
        IF purpose EQUALS `another purpose` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when such restriction constitutes a necessary, appropriate and proportionate measure within a democratic society" -- a "when" condition on a power that fails (periods ruling (b), (c)); FORK F11 (grant and power ruling item 3: listed, not changed)
        IF NOT `the restriction constitutes a necessary, appropriate and proportionate measure within a democratic society` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:148 | To this end, Member States may, inter alia, adopt legislative measures providing for the retention of data for a limited period justified on the grounds laid down in this paragraph.
@ref Art 15(1) second sentence (src:148) row:A15(1).s2
GIVEN `the measure is a legislative measure providing for the retention of data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the retention is for a limited period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the retention is justified on the grounds laid down in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(1) second sentence the Member State may adopt the legislative measure providing for the retention of data` MEANS
    IF `the measure is a legislative measure providing for the retention of data` AND `the retention is for a limited period` AND `the retention is justified on the grounds laid down in paragraph 1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a limited period justified on the grounds laid down in this paragraph" -- retention for no limited period, or on other grounds, is outside the words; and "inter alia" shows the list of measures is not closed
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:148 | All the measures referred to in this paragraph shall be in accordance with the general principles of Community law, including those referred to in Article 6(1) and (2) of the Treaty on European Union.
@ref Art 15(1) third sentence (src:148) row:A15(1).s3
GIVEN `the measure is in accordance with the general principles of Community law, including those referred to in Article 6(1) and (2) of the Treaty on European Union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(1) third sentence the measure is in accordance with the general principles of Community law` MEANS
    IF `the measure is in accordance with the general principles of Community law, including those referred to in Article 6(1) and (2) of the Treaty on European Union`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "All the measures referred to in this paragraph shall be in accordance with the general principles of Community law"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:150 | Paragraph 1 shall not apply to data specifically required by Directive 2006/24/EC
-- src:152 | to be retained for the purposes referred to in Article 1(1) of that Directive.
@ref Art 15(1a) (src:150-152) row:A15(1a)
GIVEN `the data is specifically required by Directive 2006/24/EC to be retained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be retained for the purposes referred to in Article 1(1) of that Directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(1a) paragraph 1 applies to the data` MEANS
    IF `the data is specifically required by Directive 2006/24/EC to be retained` AND `it is to be retained for the purposes referred to in Article 1(1) of that Directive`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph 1 shall not apply to data specifically required by Directive 2006/24/EC" -- FORK F4: encoded as printed; its reference may no longer have effect (the Court of Justice's judgment of 8 April 2014, checked against the Publications Office data on 2026-11-17, NOTES.md F4)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence says paragraph 1 does not apply to that data; for other data it does not say that paragraph 1 applies
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:154 | Providers shall establish internal procedures for responding to requests for access to users' personal data based on national provisions adopted pursuant to paragraph 1.
@ref Art 15(1b) first sentence (src:154) row:A15(1b).s1
GIVEN `the person is a provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(1b) first sentence the provider must establish internal procedures for responding to requests for access` MEANS
    IF `the person is a provider`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "Providers"
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the provider has established internal procedures for responding to requests for access to users' personal data based on national provisions adopted pursuant to paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(1b) first sentence the provider's duty to establish internal procedures is met` MEANS
    IF `the provider has established internal procedures for responding to requests for access to users' personal data based on national provisions adopted pursuant to paragraph 1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Providers shall establish internal procedures for responding to requests for access to users' personal data"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:154 | They shall provide the competent national authority, on demand, with information about those procedures, the number of requests received, the legal justification invoked and their response.
@ref Art 15(1b) second sentence (src:154) row:A15(1b).s2
GIVEN `the competent national authority has demanded the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(1b) second sentence the provider must provide the competent national authority with the information` MEANS
    IF `the competent national authority has demanded the information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on demand" -- an "on demand" condition that fails counts as a "where" condition (periods ruling (b), (c)); FORK F6
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the provider provided information about those procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider provided the number of requests received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider provided the legal justification invoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider provided its response` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(1b) second sentence the provider's duty to provide the information is met` MEANS
    IF `the provider provided information about those procedures` AND `the provider provided the number of requests received` AND `the provider provided the legal justification invoked` AND `the provider provided its response`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall provide the competent national authority, on demand, with information about those procedures, the number of requests received, the legal justification invoked and their response"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The text fixes no time apart from "on demand", so the rule has no WITHIN.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Directive` `Act under the Directive`
`Art 15(1b) second sentence the provider provides the authority with the information` MEANS
    PARTY `the provider`
    MUST `provide the authority with the information`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the provider` BECAUSE "Art 15(1b) second sentence: the competent national authority demanded the information and it was not provided"

-- src:156 | The provisions of Chapter III on judicial remedies, liability and sanctions of Directive 95/46/EC shall apply with regard to national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive and with regard to the individual rights derived from this Directive.
@ref Art 15(2) (src:156) row:A15(2)
GIVEN `the matter concerns national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter concerns an individual right derived from this Directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(2) Chapter III of Directive 95/46/EC on judicial remedies, liability and sanctions applies` MEANS
    IF `the matter concerns national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive` OR `the matter concerns an individual right derived from this Directive`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence says Chapter III applies "with regard to national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive" and "the individual rights derived from this Directive"; for any other matter it is silent (FORK F5: Directive 95/46/EC as printed)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:157 | The Working Party on the Protection of Individuals with regard to the Processing of Personal Data instituted by Article 29 of Directive 95/46/EC shall also carry out the tasks laid down in Article 30 of that Directive with regard to matters covered by this Directive, namely the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms and of legitimate interests in the electronic communications sector.
@ref Art 15(3) (src:157) row:A15(3)
GIVEN `the matter is covered by this Directive, namely the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms and of legitimate interests in the electronic communications sector` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(3) the Working Party carries out the tasks laid down in Article 30 of Directive 95/46/EC with regard to the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter is covered by this Directive, namely the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms and of legitimate interests in the electronic communications sector`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "matters covered by this Directive" (FORK F5: Directive 95/46/EC as printed)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Article 15a -- implementation and enforcement`

-- src:161 | Member States shall lay down the rules on penalties, including criminal sanctions where appropriate, applicable to infringements of the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive and shall take all measures necessary to ensure that they are implemented.
@ref Art 15a(1) first sentence (src:161) row:A15a(1).s1
GIVEN `the infringement is of national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15a(1) first sentence the Member State must lay down rules on penalties applicable to the infringement` MEANS
    IF `the infringement is of national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about infringements of the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the infringement is of national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `criminal sanctions are appropriate for the infringement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15a(1) first sentence the rules on penalties are to include criminal sanctions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about infringements of the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive
        IF NOT `the infringement is of national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive` THEN NOTHING
        IF `criminal sanctions are appropriate for the infringement` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "including criminal sanctions where appropriate" -- a "where" condition that fails (periods ruling (b)); the judgment of appropriateness is taken as the plain input; FORK F6
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:161 | The penalties provided for must be effective, proportionate and dissuasive and may be applied to cover the period of any breach, even where the breach has subsequently been rectified.
@ref Art 15a(1) second sentence (src:161) row:A15a(1).s2
GIVEN `the penalty is effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalty is proportionate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalty is dissuasive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15a(1) second sentence the penalty is effective, proportionate and dissuasive` MEANS
    IF `the penalty is effective` AND `the penalty is proportionate` AND `the penalty is dissuasive`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The penalties provided for must be effective, proportionate and dissuasive" -- FORK F8: "effective, proportionate and dissuasive" is the plain input
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "even where the breach has subsequently been rectified": whether the breach was rectified makes no difference, so it is not an input.
GIVEN `the penalty is applied to cover the period of the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15a(1) second sentence the penalty may be applied to cover the period of the breach, even if the breach has been rectified` MEANS
    IF `the penalty is applied to cover the period of the breach`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence says a penalty "may be applied to cover the period of any breach"; it says nothing of a penalty that does not cover the period
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:161 | The Member States shall notify those provisions to the Commission by 25 May 2011, and shall notify it without delay of any subsequent amendment affecting them.
@ref Art 15a(1) third sentence (src:161) row:A15a(1).s3
GIVEN `the date on which the Member State notified those provisions to the Commission` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15a(1) third sentence the Member State notified the provisions to the Commission in time` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the Member State notified those provisions to the Commission` GREATER THAN (Date 25 5 2011)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall notify those provisions to the Commission by 25 May 2011" -- a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling (a)); FORK F23: the last day is in time
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

GIVEN `the Member State notified the subsequent amendment without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15a(1) third sentence the Member State notified the subsequent amendment without delay` MEANS
    IF `the Member State notified the subsequent amendment without delay`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall notify it without delay of any subsequent amendment affecting them" -- FORK F9
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:162 | Without prejudice to any judicial remedy which might be available, Member States shall ensure that the competent national authority and, where relevant, other national bodies have the power to order the cessation of the infringements referred to in paragraph 1.
@ref Art 15a(2) (src:162) row:A15a(2)
GIVEN `the infringement is one referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the competent national authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is another national body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is relevant that the other national body have the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15a(2) the body must have the power to order the cessation of the infringement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about the infringements referred to in paragraph 1
        IF NOT `the infringement is one referred to in paragraph 1` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the body is the competent national authority` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the body is another national body` AND `it is relevant that the other national body have the power` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where relevant, other national bodies have the power" -- a "where" condition that fails (periods ruling (b)); the relevance is the Member State's judgment and is taken as the plain input; FORK F6
        IF `the body is another national body` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names the competent national authority and other national bodies where relevant, and is silent on any other body
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:163 | Member States shall ensure that the competent national authority and, where relevant, other national bodies have the necessary investigative powers and resources, including the power to obtain any relevant information they might need to monitor and enforce national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive.
@ref Art 15a(3) (src:163) row:A15a(3)
GIVEN `the body is the competent national authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is another national body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is relevant that the other national body have the powers and resources` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15a(3) the body must have the investigative powers and resources, including the power to obtain information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the body is the competent national authority` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the body is another national body` AND `it is relevant that the other national body have the powers and resources` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where relevant, other national bodies have the necessary investigative powers and resources" -- a "where" condition that fails (periods ruling (b)); the relevance is the Member State's judgment and is taken as the plain input; FORK F6
        IF `the body is another national body` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names the competent national authority and other national bodies where relevant, and is silent on any other body
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:164 | The relevant national regulatory authorities may adopt measures to ensure effective cross-border cooperation in the enforcement of the national laws adopted pursuant to this Directive and to create harmonised conditions for the provision of services involving cross-border data flows.
@ref Art 15a(4) first subparagraph (src:164) row:A15a(4).p1
GIVEN `the body is a relevant national regulatory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure is to ensure effective cross-border cooperation in the enforcement of the national laws adopted pursuant to this Directive or to create harmonised conditions for the provision of services involving cross-border data flows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15a(4) first subparagraph the national regulatory authority may adopt the measure` MEANS
    IF `the body is a relevant national regulatory authority` AND `the measure is to ensure effective cross-border cooperation in the enforcement of the national laws adopted pursuant to this Directive or to create harmonised conditions for the provision of services involving cross-border data flows`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("may adopt") whose gate failed (grant and power ruling item 1; FORK F13)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Article 16 -- transitional arrangements`

-- src:169 | Article 12 shall not apply to editions of directories already produced or placed on the market in printed or off-line electronic form before the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive enter into force.
@ref Art 16(1) (src:169) row:A16(1)
GIVEN `the edition was already produced or placed on the market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the edition is in printed or off-line electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that was before the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive entered into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 16(1) Article 12 applies to the edition of the directory` MEANS
    IF `the edition was already produced or placed on the market` AND `the edition is in printed or off-line electronic form` AND `that was before the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive entered into force`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Article 12 shall not apply to editions of directories already produced or placed on the market in printed or off-line electronic form before the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive enter into force"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence says Article 12 does not apply to those editions; for other editions it does not say that Article 12 applies
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:170 | Where the personal data of subscribers to fixed or mobile public voice telephony services have been included in a public subscriber directory in conformity with the provisions of Directive 95/46/EC and of Article 11 of Directive 97/66/EC before the national provisions adopted in pursuance of this Directive enter into force, the personal data of such subscribers may remain included in this public directory in its printed or electronic versions, including versions with reverse search functions, unless subscribers indicate otherwise, after having received complete information about purposes and options in accordance with Article 12 of this Directive.
@ref Art 16(2) (src:170) row:A16(2)
GIVEN `the subscriber is a subscriber to a fixed or mobile public voice telephony service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data was included in a public subscriber directory in conformity with Directive 95/46/EC and Article 11 of Directive 97/66/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that was before the national provisions adopted in pursuance of this Directive entered into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber has indicated otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber has received complete information about purposes and options in accordance with Article 12` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 16(2) the personal data of the subscriber may remain included in the public directory` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the personal data of subscribers to fixed or mobile public voice telephony services have been included in a public subscriber directory in conformity with the provisions of Directive 95/46/EC and of Article 11 of Directive 97/66/EC before the national provisions adopted in pursuance of this Directive enter into force" -- a "where" condition on a grant that fails (periods ruling (b)); FORK F11 (grant and power ruling item 3: listed, not changed)
        IF (NOT `the subscriber is a subscriber to a fixed or mobile public voice telephony service`) OR (NOT `the data was included in a public subscriber directory in conformity with Directive 95/46/EC and Article 11 of Directive 97/66/EC`) OR (NOT `that was before the national provisions adopted in pursuance of this Directive entered into force`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless subscribers indicate otherwise" -- FORK F21: this limb is tested before the information limb
        IF `the subscriber has indicated otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after having received complete information about purposes and options in accordance with Article 12" -- a named complement of the grant, not met
        IF NOT `the subscriber has received complete information about purposes and options in accordance with Article 12` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 19 -- repeal: how references to the repealed Directive read`

-- src:182 | References made to the repealed Directive shall be construed as being made to this Directive.
@ref Art 19 second subparagraph (src:182) row:A19.p2
GIVEN `the reference is made to Directive 97/66/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 19 second subparagraph the reference is construed as made to this Directive` MEANS
    IF `the reference is made to Directive 97/66/EC`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about references made to the repealed Directive; for any other reference it is silent
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Article 21 -- addressees`

-- src:188 | This Directive is addressed to the Member States.
@ref Art 21 (src:188) row:A21
GIVEN `the body is a Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 21 the Directive is addressed to the body` MEANS
    IF `the body is a Member State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names the Member States as the addressees; it does not say in so many words that nobody else is bound by the rules it states for providers, senders and subscribers, and whether a rule has direct effect is not decided in this row
    ELSE NOTHING
